1
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:09,240
Imagine making plans to
watch a TV programme.

2
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:12,440
You check the time of your show,

3
00:00:12,660 --> 00:00:15,800
then you wait hours, days or even weeks

4
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:19,320
because it will be shown exactly once.

5
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:25,880
That is the way the parents of
today’s teenagers used to watch TV.

6
00:00:26,980 --> 00:00:31,880
Of course, all that changed when
on-demand streaming services appeared.

7
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:37,580
Today, we don’t even have to wait
for new episodes to be released.

8
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:43,480
In 2013, Netflix released
all thirteen episodes

9
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:46,340
of the first season of House of Cards
together.

10
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:52,020
This decision completely changed
the way we consume content.

11
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:57,140
Now you come home from school,

12
00:00:57,140 --> 00:01:02,380
and simply download the series
your friends say is a must-see TV show.

13
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:10,240
Soon, it’s past your bedtime, and
you’ve already watched seven episodes.

14
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,580
Just one more, you promise yourself…

15
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:17,120
Binge-watching

16
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:21,300
is the practice of watching many
episodes of a show back-to-back.

17
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:27,160
It is made easier by the fact that
on-demand streaming services

18
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:32,760
have hundreds of shows to choose from,
the latest ones and the classic ones.

19
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:35,960
A survey by Netflix

20
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:41,980
found that over 70% of people connected
binge-watching with positive feelings.

21
00:01:42,580 --> 00:01:45,120
It helps us connect with other people.

22
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:49,580
When a large number of people
watch the same show,

23
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:53,900
they are able to relate with each other
and share what they think about it.

24
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:59,500
Today, you can discuss a popular show
with your close friend at school

25
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:02,840
and fans of the show from
another part of the world.

26
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:08,300
Binge-watching programmes once in a while
can help us reduce stress.

27
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:13,980
It helps us to relax and stop thinking
about school or problems we may have.

28
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:20,200
But there are clear disadvantages, too.

29
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:26,220
Watching TV for hours on end can lead
to physical health problems,

30
00:02:26,220 --> 00:02:27,740
like weight gain,

31
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:30,120
low energy,

32
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:34,240
or poor quality of sleep.

33
00:02:38,020 --> 00:02:41,100
Binge-watching can also cause
mental health issues,

34
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:45,240
such as stress because you feel guilty
that you have wasted time

35
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:48,440
you could spend doing something
useful or active.

36
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:53,280
It also causes feelings of sadness
when a show ends,

37
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:56,180
and anxiety about
what will replace it.

38
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,760
Binge-watching is a form of addiction.

39
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:04,960
To ensure that we don’t let
binge-watching affect our health,

40
00:03:05,340 --> 00:03:07,580
we can set ourselves a time limit,

41
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:12,700
stop eating unhealthy snacks
while watching shows,

42
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:17,080
and make sure that we exercise regularly

43
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:22,260
and have conversations
about the real world.

44
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:28,420
With these simple habits,
we can continue enjoying shows

45
00:03:28,420 --> 00:03:31,580
and stay in good physical
and mental health.
